Path parameters
    separated by forward slashes /
    Mandatory,Identify a specific resource,
    Hierarchical Relationships
        https://api.example.com/users/42/orders/105
    Best Practices:
        Use meaningful names 
        never put sensitive data like passwords or API keys

    @app.get("/items/{item_id}")
    def read_item(item_id: int):

    @app.get("/files/{file_path:path}")
    def read_file(file_path: str):



Query Parameters:
    optional,used to filter, sort, paginate, or search
    Appended after ?,    Separated by &
    Key-Value Format
    Multiple Parameters:
        https://api.example.com/products?status=active&sort=price_asc&page=2&limit=20
    @app.get("/items/")
    def read_items(skip: int = 0, limit: int = 10):

    @app.get("/users/{user_id}/items/{item_id}")
    def read_user_item(    user_id: int,     item_id: str, 
    q: Union[str, None] = None,     short: bool = False):

route definitions:
    @app.get("/items/")
    def get_items():
        return {"message": "Get all items"}

    @app.post("/items/")
    def create_item():
        return {"message": "Create a new item"}

    @app.put("/items/{item_id}")
    def update_item(item_id: int):
        return {"message": f"Update item {item_id}"}

    @app.delete("/items/{item_id}")
    def delete_item(item_id: int):
        return {"message": f"Delete item {item_id}"}

